      "factual_description": "Jazz at Lincoln Center presents Paquito D’Rivera Plays the Music of Chick Corea on March 12–13, 2027 at 7:30 PM in Rose Theater. Conceived by conductor Josep Vicent with arrangements by Emilio Solla, the U.S. debut concert combines symphony orchestra and jazz ensemble to reimagine Chick Corea works including Spain and Armando's Rhumba, with D’Rivera as special guest. The program takes inspiration from the recorded project The Chick Corea Symphony Tribute. Ritmo.",
